{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/trackingplans"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"metadata":{"externalID":"TrackingPlans","roleHeading":"Framework","symbolKind":"module","role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"TrackingPlans"}],"title":"TrackingPlans"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Making-a-plan","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/File","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanError"],"title":"Making a plan"},{"anchor":"Writing-a-plan","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/files","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/files(carryingForward:)","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/write(to:)","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanCommand"],"title":"Writing a plan"},{"anchor":"Checking-a-plan","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/check(against:)","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/check(againstDirectory:)","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanCheck","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanDifference"],"title":"Checking a plan"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/JSON"],"anchor":"Enumerations","title":"Enumerations"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Export every event an app tracks as JSON Schema that people and services outside the app can read, and check each change against the plan committed before it."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A tracking plan is the contract between an app and whoever reads its events: dashboards, a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"warehouse, a collector, another platform’s client. Each event’s document gives its version,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"consent category, properties and their JSON types, which ones every payload holds, and which are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", in a form that needs no Swift to read. Committed beside the events, it puts every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"change to them in the pull request as a JSON diff. Its check says which changes break what has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"already shipped: payloads from installed app versions that a validating collector would reject,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and stored records the app could no longer decode.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" turns events’ schemas into files: an index, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tracking-plan.json"},{"type":"text","text":", and for each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event a JSON Schema (draft 2020-12) document and an example payload. The files are values, so the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same schemas give the same bytes on every run and platform, ready to commit for the people and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tools outside the app."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Checking compares the plan the events make now with the committed one by what the files mean. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanCheck","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is a match, a plan that is only out of date, or one with a breaking","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"difference: a change that, at the same version, would leave a stored record or an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"already-released app’s payload unable to decode or validate. Each ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanDifference","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" names","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the event, the property and the change, and says whether it is breaking.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Only code compiled against the app’s event types can read their schemas, so the app writes a small","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"executable of its own: a type that conforms to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanCommand","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", marked ","type":"text"},{"code":"@main","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". It writes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the plan to a directory, or checks it with ","type":"text"},{"code":"check","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". To run the check from the app’s tests instead,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"use ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlanTesting","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The schemas usually come from ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventMacros","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"):","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/init()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" takes every ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in the program and the library’s own events, found at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"run time, and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/init(schemas:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" takes a list.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The module is a product of its own that ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" leaves out.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import TrackingPlans","import Traffluent","","@Event(name: \"signed_up\")","struct SignedUp {","    var plan: String","}","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()  \/\/ every @Event in the program, and the library's own","let check = plan.check(against: plan.files)  \/\/ .matches","let paths = plan.files.map(\\.path)","\/\/ [\"tracking-plan.json\", ..., \"signed_up.v1.schema.json\", \"signed_up.v1.example.json\"]"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingplanworkflow","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers the executable, the command plugins and the test.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://TrackingPlans/documentation/TrackingPlans/JSON/minified":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The value as JSON text with no whitespace between its tokens, object keys in the order of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"their UTF-8 bytes, as JavaScript’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"JSON.stringify(value)"},{"type":"text","text":" writes it: a request body. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/JSON\/number(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" that is NaN or infinite is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentatio